<title>SPAIN: Madrid airport back to normal after lightning hit.</title>
<headline>Madrid airport back to normal after lightning hit.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Madrid's Barajas airport returned to normal on Tuesday after an antenna was struck by lightning causing delays, airport authority Aena said.</p>
<p>The airport stemmed the flow of departing planes for 30 minutes this morning when a bolt of lightning damaged an antenna at a nearby control point during a freak storm. Arrivals were not affected.</p>
<p>Flights were delayed for a further two hours, but by midday planes were departing on time again. A total of 800 flights are scheduled to pass through the airport on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
